# Extraction test fixtures and their captured snapshots must always be
# checked out with LF line endings, regardless of the checkout platform or a
# user's core.autocrlf setting (Git-for-Windows defaults to true, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout for anything Git considers "text").
#
# These files are position-sensitive: the fixture sources are fed straight
# into tree-sitter/libclang, and a CRLF byte at a line end shifts every
# downstream column position and can inject a stray "\r" into captured
# multi-line text (e.g. tagged_scope). A CRLF checkout would corrupt them
# independently of anything the test harness does at run time. They are also
# mirrored byte-for-byte into a second implementation's test suite, so a
# platform-dependent checkout would break that comparison too, not only
# Windows CI here.
#
# Scoped to the test-data/snapshot trees that actually encode positions or
# get byte-compared, not the whole repository, so this can't churn unrelated
# files the way a blanket `* text=auto` would.
tests/data/** text eol=lf
tests/__snapshots__/** text eol=lf
